      {
        "content": "Caroline has 40 pairs of socks. She loses 4 pairs of socks at the laundromat. Of the remaining pairs of socks, she donates two-thirds to the thrift store. Then she purchases 10 new pairs of socks, and she receives 3 new pairs of socks as a gift from her dad. How many pairs of socks does Caroline have in total?",
        "role": "user"
      },
      {
        "content": " FINAL: 21",
        "role": "assistant"
      },
      {
        "content": "Given:\n- Caroline starts with 40 pairs of socks.\n- She loses 4 pairs at the laundromat.\n- She donates two-thirds of the remaining pairs to the thrift store.\n- She then purchases 10 new pairs.\n- She receives 3 new pairs as a gift.\n\nUnknown:\n- The total number of pairs of socks Caroline has after these events.\n\nStep-by-step solution:\n1. After losing 4 pairs, Caroline has \\(40 - 4 = 36\\) pairs.\n2. She donates two-thirds of the remaining pairs: \\(\\frac{2}{3} \\times 36 = 24\\) pairs.\n3. After the donation, she has \\(36 - 24 = 12\\) pairs.\n4. She then purchases 10 new pairs, so she has \\(12 + 10 = 22\\) pairs.\n5. She receives 3 more pairs as a gift, so she has \\(22 + 3 = 25\\) pairs.\n\nThe final number of pairs of socks Caroline has is 25.\n\nFINAL: 25",
        "role": "assistant"
      },
      {
